        <p class="profile-detail-region">Life · Egypt &amp; North Africa</p>
        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Hannibal</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Period</span><span class="info-stat-val">247 BCE – c. 183 BCE</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Born</span><span class="info-stat-val">247 BCE, most likely in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carthage">Carthage</a>; son of the Carthaginian general and statesman <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hamilcar-barca">Hamilcar Barca</a>, whose descendants are known as the Barcids</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Died</span><span class="info-stat-val">Between 183 and 181 BCE, at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/libyssa">Libyssa</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bithynia">Bithynia</a>; according to Cornelius Nepos and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/livy">Livy</a> he took poison when Roman soldiers surrounded the castle where he lived, though the precise year and cause are unknown</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Who they were</span><span class="info-stat-val">Officer under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hasdrubal-the-fair">Hasdrubal the Fair</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hispania">Hispania</a>; commander-in-chief of the Carthaginian army in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iberia">Iberia</a> from 221 BCE; commander against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> in the Second Punic War; suffete (chief magistrate) of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carthage">Carthage</a> after the war; military adviser to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antiochus-iii-the-great">Antiochus III</a> and commander for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prusias-i-of-bithynia">Prusias I of Bithynia</a></span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Known for</span><span class="info-stat-val">The oath never to be a friend of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>; the crossing of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alps">Alps</a> with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-elephant">war elephants</a>; the victories at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trebbia">Trebia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-trasimeno">Lake Trasimene</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-cannae">Cannae</a>; fifteen years of war in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>; the defeat at Zama by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scipio-africanus">Scipio Africanus</a>; financial and political reforms at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carthage">Carthage</a>; exile and death by poison</span></div>
        </div>
