    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>Hannibal took command of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carthage">Carthage</a>'s army in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iberia">Iberia</a> at 26, attacked <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>'s ally <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sagunto">Saguntum</a> and carried the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-punic-war">Second Punic War</a> into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> by crossing the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alps">Alps</a> in 218 BCE.</li><li>At <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-cannae">Cannae</a> in 216 BCE he surrounded and destroyed a larger Roman army, yet he could not take <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>, received little support from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carthage">Carthage</a> and was worn down over fifteen years in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>.</li><li>Defeated at Zama in 202 BCE, he reformed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carthage">Carthage</a>'s finances as suffete, was driven into exile by his enemies and by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>, and took poison in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bithynia">Bithynia</a> rather than be surrendered.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>While wintering among the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gauls">Gauls</a> of northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>, Hannibal feared that tribesmen would try to assassinate him to win back <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>'s favour, and took to altering his appearance with differently dyed wigs so that they would not recognise him.</p></aside>
    </section>

